<title>GERMANY: Berlin airports air cargo rises 4.6pct in Feb 97.</title>
<headline>Berlin airports air cargo rises 4.6pct in Feb 97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total flown air cargo handled at the three Berlin airports, Tegel, Schoenefeld and Tempelhof, in February rose 4.6 percent to 2,774 tonnes, figures from the German airports association ADV showed.</p>
<p>This was a fall on the 16.8 percent growth recorded in January, the monthly ADV traffic report showed.</p>
<p>The following tables show cargo handled at the Berlin airports in February and for the year to date in tonnes and with year-on-year percentage changes.</p>
<p>    Feb 1997			Monthly total	Pct change</p>
<p>    Total flown cargo		2,774		Up    4.6</p>
<p>    Exports			    1,095		Up    5.2</p>
<p>    Imports			    1,412		Down  3.8</p>
<p>    Transit				267			n/a</p>
<p>    Jan-Feb 1997		 Cumulative total    Pct change</p>
<p>    Total flown cargo		5,522		Up   10.3</p>
<p>    Exports			    2,078		Up    8.3</p>
<p>    Imports			    2,942		Up    4.5</p>
<p>    Transit				502			n/a</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research dept.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
</text>
